Experimental DXIL (Shader Model 6.x) front end in airconv: the DXIL bitcode is read with
airconv's LLVM 15, moved into the AIR module and the dx.op calls are lowered to AIR.
Resources from !dx.resources fill the same ShaderInfo as DXBC SM 5.1, signatures go
through the DXBC signature handlers (synthesized dcl instructions), so root signature
binding, vertex pulling and outputs are shared. Vertex, pixel and compute shaders;
SM 6.6 dynamic resources (ResourceDescriptorHeap, root signature *_HEAP_DIRECTLY_INDEXED:
the command list writes the heap addresses after the root parameters), wave and quad
ops, 64-bit min/max atomics (AIR 2.9 module, macOS 27). D3D12 UAV textures get the
shader atomic usage. Command list markers and predication no longer abort. airconv CLI
uses an embedded root signature. No GS/HS/DS/mesh, no 16-bit types, no doubles.

